{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And YHWH blessed the Egyptian's house for Joseph's sake.</b> Scripture compared him to the Ark of the Covenant, concerning which it is written (II Samuel 6:11): ״וישב ארון ה' בית עובד אדום הגתי ג' חדשים ויברך ה' את עובד אדום ואת כל ביתו״." "<b>In the house.</b> This is the blessing of the house — in money and in vessels. <b>And in the field.</b> In grain crops and in fruits and in plantings. Until now he was accountable with a reckoning; from here onward without reckoning, as it says: ״ויעזוב את כל אשר לו ביד יוסף״." "<b>And in the Midrash.</b> 'In the house and in the field' — in the house six months in winter, and in the field six months in summer. From here you learn that Joseph remained in the house of Potiphar one year, and in the prison house twelve years, for we find thirteen years from when he parted from his father until he ruled in Egypt. And his time to go forth from the authority of Potiphar was at the end of eleven years, according to the reckoning of eleven sheaves in the first dream and eleven stars in the second dream, except that two years were added to him as punishment for two words, which are: והזכרתני and הוצאתני."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 39, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:18:50.399448345Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}